{:edb/committed true :edb/basis-t 2587 :edb/replayed false :edb/tx-hash "4bd27eb94ef929d8281dcbb29c2d19e65a23c8560d4175cf2c0879dcb55a4ea2" :edb/db-before-t 2586 :edb/db-after-t 2587 :edb/tx-data [[13194139535899 50 #inst "2026-10-09T10:10:39.417Z" 13194139535899 true] [17592186124407 1020 #edb/ref 17592186373298 13194139535899 true] [17592186124407 1020 #edb/ref 17592186373305 13194139535899 true] [17592186124407 1020 #edb/ref 17592186373326 13194139535899 true] [17592186124408 1020 #edb/ref 17592186373312 13194139535899 true] [17592186124408 1020 #edb/ref 17592186373319 13194139535899 true] [17592186373298 1017 #edb/ref 17592186373299 13194139535899 true] [17592186373298 1089 "q-107347" 13194139535899 true] [17592186373298 1091 #edb/ref 17592186045463 13194139535899 true] [17592186373298 1100 "Consider the vector space ${\\text{M}}_{2}(R)$ of all $2\\times 2$ matrices over $R.$\n\nWhich of the following statements are true?\n\n- ${[\\begin{aligned}0 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 0\\end{aligned}],[\\begin{aligned}1 & 0 \\\\ 0 & -1\\end{aligned}],[\\begin{aligned}0 & -1 \\\\ 1 & 0\\end{aligned}]}$ is a linearly independent set in ${\\text{M}}_{2}(R)$\n- $[\\begin{aligned}2 & 3 \\\\ -3 & -2\\end{aligned}]$ can be expressed as a linear combination of ${[\\begin{aligned}0 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 0\\end{aligned}],[\\begin{aligned}1 & 0 \\\\ 0 & -1\\end{aligned}],[\\begin{aligned}0 & -1 \\\\ 1 & 0\\end{aligned}]}$\n- ${[\\begin{aligned}0 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 0\\end{aligned}],[\\begin{aligned}1 & 0 \\\\ 0 & -1\\end{aligned}],[\\begin{aligned}0 & -1 \\\\ 1 & 0\\end{aligned}]}$ is a basis of ${\\text{M}}_{2}(R)$" 13194139535899 true] [17592186373298 1113 #uuid "40a13f26-f6cb-5a20-8304-cddf840ba5f5" 13194139535899 true] [17592186373298 1145 "Let's examine each of the statements in turn.\n\n- Statement I is false. Notice that\n\n$$\n1\\cdot [\\begin{aligned}0 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 0\\end{aligned}]+0\\cdot [\\begin{aligned}1 & 0 \\\\ 0 & -1\\end{aligned}]+0\\cdot [\\begin{aligned}0 & -1 \\\\ 1 & 0\\end{aligned}]=[\\begin{aligned}0 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 0\\end{aligned}]\n$$\n\nwhere the first coefficient is nonzero, so the set is linearly dependent. In general, any set that contains a zero-matrix is linearly dependent.\n\n- Statement II is true. Indeed,\n\n$$\n[\\begin{aligned}2 & 3 \\\\ -3 & 2\\end{aligned}]=0\\cdot [\\begin{aligned}0 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 0\\end{aligned}]+2\\cdot [\\begin{aligned}1 & 0 \\\\ 0 & -1\\end{aligned}]+(-3)\\cdot [\\begin{aligned}0 & -1 \\\\ 1 & 0\\end{aligned}].\n$$\n\n- Statement III is false. Since the set is not linearly independent, it can't form a basis.\n\nTherefore, the correct answer is \"II only.\"" 13194139535899 true] [17592186373299 1000 #edb/ref 17592186373300 13194139535899 true] [17592186373299 1000 #edb/ref 17592186373301 13194139535899 true] [17592186373299 1000 #edb/ref 17592186373302 13194139535899 true] [17592186373299 1000 #edb/ref 17592186373303 13194139535899 true] [17592186373299 1000 #edb/ref 17592186373304 13194139535899 true] [17592186373299 1040 #edb/ref 17592186045450 13194139535899 true] [17592186373299 1041 "selection" 13194139535899 true] [17592186373299 1104 #edb/ref 17592186373304 13194139535899 true] [17592186373299 1110 #uuid "1e01aebd-792b-50da-9365-d460626ced01" 13194139535899 true] [17592186373300 1034 "II and III only" 13194139535899 true] [17592186373300 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045454 13194139535899 true] [17592186373300 1111 #uuid "4fed9504-8458-5ef4-9542-7bdb365aa1b8" 13194139535899 true] [17592186373301 1034 "I only" 13194139535899 true] [17592186373301 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045454 13194139535899 true] [17592186373301 1111 #uuid "5659bee5-e675-5242-b4fa-cbbd9f53fd13" 13194139535899 true] [17592186373302 1034 "III only" 13194139535899 true] [17592186373302 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045454 13194139535899 true] [17592186373302 1111 #uuid "5039b09c-f358-5a53-b3da-33187e30007e" 13194139535899 true] [17592186373303 1034 "I and II only" 13194139535899 true] [17592186373303 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045454 13194139535899 true] [17592186373303 111